# What stays out of the Git repository.
#
# The repository holds the code, the documentation, the sample and the three
# small tables, so that it can be read and cloned in seconds. The complete
# package, sensors included, lives on Zenodo under its DOI. README.md says
# which is which.

# 389 MB in 495 files: too large for Git, and Git LFS does not help, because the
# free bandwidth quota is 1 GB a month and one clone of this is a third of it.
data/sensors/

# Derived tables, 2.5 MB. Reproduced exactly by code/features.py from the
# published events, so versioning them would only invite them to drift.
data/features/

# Release artefacts, built by code/make_release_zip.py
*.zip

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Editors and operating systems
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
